# Kea DHCPv4 per Portitor instance (portitor-kea4@.service). The AppArmor
# profile for kea-dhcp4 on Debian/Ubuntu only allows Kea's own file names;
# install.py adds these rules to the profile's local include
# (/etc/apparmor.d/local/usr.sbin.kea-dhcp4). The paths are the defaults of
# etc_dir, kea_data_dir and kea_socket_dir in /etc/portitor/agent.yaml, and
# the unit's KEA_PIDFILE_DIR and KEA_LOCKFILE_DIR.
/etc/portitor/instances/*/kea-dhcp4.conf r,
/var/lib/kea/kea-leases4-*.csv* rwk,
/run/kea/kea4-*.sock rw,
/run/kea/kea4-*.sock.lock rwk,
/run/kea/*/ r,
/run/kea/*/kea-dhcp4.kea-dhcp4.pid rwk,
/run/kea/*/logger_lockfile rwk,
